ss><country>KR</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SEJU ENGINEERING CO LTD</name><address><country>KR</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>CHUNG, HAN</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>LEE, HO-JUN</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>LEE, WON-BAE</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEJU ENGINEERING CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>CHUNG HAN</name><address><country>KR</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>LEE HO-JUN</name><address><country>KR</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>LEE WON-BAE</name><address><country>KR</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>CHUNG, HAN</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>LEE, HO-JUN</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>LEE, WON-BAE</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An ulatraminiaturized reserve battery cell the whole size of which is as small as several millimeters and which includes small battery components the sizes of which are several micrometers and is fabricated by micromachining for machining a mechanical structure to a very small size, so as to complement the drawbacks of existing large reserve battery cells which can be hardly used for small electronic systems. An electrolyte jar and other battery components are realized by using materials such as silicon, nickel, copper, and aluminum. The electrolyte jar containing an electrolyte in contact with the battery cell has a membrane structure having a smaller thickness than that of the periphery. Only at the activation, the structure is broken to ensure sufficient impact resistance strength in normal use and to activate the battery with small power.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une pile de réserve ultra-miniaturisée dont les dimensions hors-tout sont de l'ordre de quelques millimètres seulement et qui comprend de petits composants de batterie dont les dimensions sont de l'ordre de quelques micromètres. On fabrique cette pile par micro-usinage de manière à obtenir une structure mécanique de très petites dimensions, ce qui permet de pallier les défauts des piles de réserve existantes, de grandes dimensions, qui ne peuvent guère être utilisées dans de petits systèmes électroniques. On fabrique la cuve d'électrolyte et les autres composants de la pile avec des matériaux tels que le silicium, le nickel, le cuivre et l'aluminium. La cuve d'électrolyte contenant un électrolyte en contact avec la pile possède une structure à membrane dont l'épaisseur est inférieure à celle de la périphérie. La structure n'est rompue qu'au moment de l'activation, ce qui permet d'assurer une force suffisante de résistance à l'impact en cours d'utilisation normale et d'activer la batterie avec une puissance peu élevée.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>